nly suffix automaton then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" transform to some of its subsequence. Checking that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a subsequence of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be performed in different ways. Easiest and fastest — well-known two pointers method. In case of using suffix array we can get every permutation of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If it is not obvious for you, try to think. Thus, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be anagrams. If we count number of each letter in each string, we can check this. If every letter appears in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the same times as in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" then words are anagrams. In case of using both structures strategy is: remove some letters and shuffle the rest. It is possible if every letter appears in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" not less times than in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Otherwise it is impossible to make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Total complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + 26)."}],"k